### HAML Class Attributes Rules

#### When to Check These Rules
- When writing or modifying HAML templates
- When adding or modifying Tailwind classes
- When working with dynamic class attributes

#### Rules
- Never use arbitrary values (square brackets) directly in HAML class attributes
- For Tailwind classes, use one of these two approaches:
  1. Define custom classes in Tailwind config and reference them directly:
     ```haml
     .grid.grid-cols-service-provider
     ```
  2. Use HAML's attribute syntax with curly braces for dynamic classes:
     ```haml
     .grid{ class: "grid-cols-[#{dynamic_value}]" }
     ```
- When combining multiple classes, use HAML's class attribute syntax:
  ```haml
  .base-class{ class: "additional-class" }
  ```

#### Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Using raw class strings with square brackets
- Mixing static and dynamic classes incorrectly
- Not using proper HAML attribute syntax

#### Validation Checklist
- [ ] No direct square bracket usage in class attributes
- [ ] Dynamic classes use proper HAML syntax
- [ ] Custom Tailwind classes are defined in config
- [ ] Class combinations use proper syntax
